<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"8ad64841","external_id":"607e02b9-ac5b-48d2-8d14-a74f33743cd9","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"f6fe5c8c-407f-4533-a7d4-6963dd89b0e4","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.B.","skill_desc":"Linear functions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A linear function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> gives a company&rsquo;s profit, in dollars, for selling <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> items. The company&rsquo;s profit is <math alttext=\"dollar sign 220\"><mo>$</mo><mrow><mn>220</mn></mrow></math> when it sells <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> items, and its profit is <math alttext=\"dollar sign 320\"><mo>$</mo><mrow><mn>320</mn></mrow></math> when it sells <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math> items. Which equation defines <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"0f7d9686-4802-47eb-bc67-6212fe679d13","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 150 x minus 320\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>150</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>320</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"011e5e18-ce9a-4bc0-85f3-37a8685fb03e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 32 x\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"bd8bf100-575c-4342-8bf1-b470c9afb65e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 50 x minus 10 x\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"17593647-e40d-452c-b76c-9b1767772647","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 50 x minus 180\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>180</mn></mrow></math></p>"}],"keys":["17593647-e40d-452c-b76c-9b1767772647"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the relationship between <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is linear. A linear function can be written in the form <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals m x plus b\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math> is the slope and <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph of <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane. Given two points on a line, <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x 1 comma y 1 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> and&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis x 2 comma y 2 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>, the slope of the line can be found using the slope formula <math alttext=\"m equals StartFraction y 2 minus y 1 Over x 2 minus x 1 EndFraction\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the company&rsquo;s profit is <math alttext=\"dollar sign 220\"><mo>$</mo><mn>220</mn></math> when it sells <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> items and the profit is <math alttext=\"dollar sign 320\"><mo>$</mo><mn>320</mn></math> when it sells <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math> items. Since&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> represents the company's profit, in dollars, for selling <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> items, the graph of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane passes through the points <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 8 comma 220 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>220</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 10 comma 320 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>320</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 8 comma 220 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>220</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 10 comma 320 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>320</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> for&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis x 1 comma y 1 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x 2 comma y 2 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>, respectively, in the&nbsp;slope formula yields <math alttext=\"m equals StartFraction 320 minus 220 Over 10 minus 8 EndFraction\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>320</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>220</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, which gives <math alttext=\"m equals StartFraction 100 Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"m equals 50\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>m</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>50</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"220\"><mn>220</mn>\n</math> for&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals m x plus b\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"220 equals left parenthesis 50 right parenthesis left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis plus b\"><mn>220</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mn>50</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>8</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, or <math alttext=\"220 equals 400 plus b\"><mn>220</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"400\"><mn>400</mn>\n</math> from each side of this equation yields <math alttext=\"negative 180 equals b\"><mo>-</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"negative 180\"><mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mn>180</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> in <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals m x plus b\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 50 x minus 180\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>180</mn></math>. Therefore, the equation that defines <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 50 x minus 180\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>180</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357388,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"8ad64841","skill_cd":"H.B.","score_band_range_cd":5,"skill_desc":"Linear functions","createDate":1730147357388,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"","external_id":"607e02b9-ac5b-48d2-8d14-a74f33743cd9","primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"f6fe5c8c-407f-4533-a7d4-6963dd89b0e4","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 150 x minus 320\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>150</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>320</mn></mrow></math></p>","id":"0f7d9686-4802-47eb-bc67-6212fe679d13"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 32 x\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></math></p>","id":"011e5e18-ce9a-4bc0-85f3-37a8685fb03e"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 50 x minus 10 x\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi></math></p>","id":"bd8bf100-575c-4342-8bf1-b470c9afb65e"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 50 x minus 180\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>180</mn></mrow></math></p>","id":"17593647-e40d-452c-b76c-9b1767772647"}],"externalid":"607e02b9-ac5b-48d2-8d14-a74f33743cd9","keys":["17593647-e40