nse budget for one year is <span class="italic">x</span> million dollars. It follows then that the expression <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8adf1335/img_005_47e837ca.png" alt="y plus 201"></span> is equivalent to <span class="italic">x</span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8adf1335/img_006_a7fe0265.png" alt="y plus 201, equals x"></span>. Subtracting <span class="italic">y</span> from both sides of this equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8adf1335/img_007_b7020b2c.png" alt="201 equals, x minus y"></span>. By the symmetric property of equality, this is the same as <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8adf1335/img_008_acecbc76.png" alt="x minus y, equals 201"></span>.<p>Choices A and C are incorrect. Because it&rsquo;s given that the total expense budget for one year, <span class="italic">x</span> million dollars, is comprised of the departmental expenses, <span class="italic">y</span> million dollars, and all other expenses, 201 million dollars, the expressions <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8adf1335/img_009_5d562a08.png" alt="x plus y"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8adf1335/img_010_3917cff8.png" alt="2 x minus y  "></span> both must be equivalent to a value greater than 201 million dollars. Therefore, the equations <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8adf1335/img_011_627ca784.png" alt="x plus y, equals 201 "></span>and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8adf1335/img_012_d8ed96dd.png" alt="2 x minus y, equals 201 "></span>aren&rsquo;t true. Choice D is incorrect. The value of <span class="italic">x </span>must be greater than the value of <span class="italic">y</span>. Therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8adf1335/img_013_4ed298d9.png" alt="y minus x, equals 201"></span> can&rsquo;t represent this relationship.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
