expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"99 degrees Fahrenheit\"></span></span>, inclusive. If Kevin, an adult male, has a body temperature that is considered to be normal, which of the following could be his body temperature?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"96 point 7 degrees Fahrenheit\"></span></span></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"97 point 6 degrees Fahrenheit\"></span></span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"97 point 9 degrees Fahrenheit\"></span></span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"99 point 7 degrees Fahrenheit\"></span></span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"c","rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. Normal body temperature must be greater than or equal to 97.8&deg;F but less than or equal to 99&deg;F. Of the given choices, 97.9&deg;F is the only temperature that fits these restrictions.<p>Choices A and B are incorrect. These temperatures are less than 97.8&deg;F, so they don&rsquo;t fit the given restrictions. Choice D is incorrect. This temperature is greater than 99&deg;F, so it doesn&rsquo;t fit the given restrictions.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959618,"updateDate":1691007959618}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959618, 1691007959618),
    ($SATQ$92aa3a94$SATQ$, $SATQ$7840df29-5b0a-4ae4-9fb1-c8f458684f0b$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear equations in two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Line <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math> is defined by <math alttext="y equals 7 x plus one eighth"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>7</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mfrac>
			<mn>1</mn>
			<mn>8</mn>
		</mfrac>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Line <math alttext="j"><mi>j</mi>
</math> is perpendicular to line <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane. What is the slope of line <math alttext="j"><mi>j</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"1fea85ef-8a35-45df-886e-f3adab757a7d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 8\"><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2fd0297b-7280-443b-9883-255c22de45cf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative one seventh\"><mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"107efcf9-ee8b-4276-9e0a-6b5b456cd607","content":"<p><math alttext=\"one eighth\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t<mn>8</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c6d23d05-aa1b-4535-b999-769db380832b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["2fd0297b-7280-443b-9883-255c22de45cf"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. It's given that line <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math> is defined by <math alttext="y equals 7 x plus one eighth"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>. For an equation in slope-intercept form <math alttext="y equals m x plus b"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, <math alttext="m"><mi>m</mi>
</math> represents the slope of the line defined by this equation in the <em>xy</em>-plane and <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> represents the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of this line. Therefore, the slope of line <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math>. It&rsquo;s also given that line <math alttext="j"><mi>j</mi>
</math> is perpendicular to line <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane. Therefore, the slope of line <math alttext="j"><mi>j</mi>
</math> is the opposite reciprocal of the slope of line <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math>. The opposite reciprocal of <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math> is <math alttext="negative one seventh"><mrow>
	<mo>-</mo>
	<mfrac>
		<mn>1</mn>
		<mn>7</mn>
	</mfrac>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the slope of line <math alttext="j"><mi>j</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="negative one seventh"><mrow>
	<mo>-</mo>
	<mfrac>
		<mn>1</mn>
		<mn>7</mn>
	</mfrac>
</mrow>
</math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the opposite reciprocal of the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept, not the slope, of line <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math>.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of line <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math>, not the slope of line <math alttext="j"><mi>j</mi>
</math>.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the slope of a line that is parallel, not perpendicular, to line <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"92aa3a94","external_id":"7840df29-5b0a-4ae4-9fb1-c8f458684f0b","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"94a66875-9ae9-42db-a0cd-f824cc3f7c3e","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.C.","skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> is defined by <math alttext=\"y equals 7 x plus one eighth\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t</mfrac>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Line <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math> is perpendicular to line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane. What is the slope of line <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"1fea85ef-8a35-45df-886e-f3adab757a7d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 8\"><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2fd0297b-7280-443b-9883-255c22de45cf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative one seventh\"><mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"107efcf9-ee8b-4276-9e0a-6b5b456cd607","content":"<p><math alttext=\"one eighth\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t<mn>8</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c6d23d05-aa1b-4535-b999-769db380832b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["2fd0297b-7280-443b-9883-255c22de45cf"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. It's given that line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> is defined by <math alttext=\"y equals 7 x plus one eighth\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>. For an equation in slope-intercept form <math alttext=\"y equals m x plus b\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math> represents the slope of the line defined by this equation in the <em>xy</em>-plane and <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> represents the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of this line. Therefore, the slope of line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s also given that line <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math> is perpendicular to line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane. Therefore, the slope of line <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math> is the opposite reciprocal of the slope of line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math>. The opposite reciprocal of <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"negative one seventh\"><mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the slope of line <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"negative one seventh\"><mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the opposite reciprocal of the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept, not the slope, of line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math>, not the slope of line <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the slope of a line that is parallel, not perpendicular, to line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357392,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"92aa3a94","skill_cd":"H.C.","score_band_range_cd":5,"skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","createDate":1730147357392,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"","external_id":"7840df29-5b0a-4ae4-9fb1-c8f458684f0b","primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"94a66875-9ae9-42db-a0cd-f824cc3f7c3e","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 8\"><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"1fea85ef-8a35-45df-886e-f3adab757a7d"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative one seventh\"><mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>","id":"2fd0297b-7280-443b-9883-255c22de45cf"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"one eighth\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t<mn>8</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>","id":"107efcf9-ee8b-4276-9e0a-6b5b456cd607"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"c6d23d05-aa1b-4535-b999-769db380832b"}],"externalid":"7840df29-5b0a-4ae4-9fb1-c8f458684f0b","keys":["2fd0297b-7280-443b-9883-255c22de45cf"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. It's given that line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> is defined by <math alttext=\"y equals 7 x plus one eighth\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>. For an equation in slope-intercept form <math alttext=\"y equals m x plus b\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math> represents the slope of the line defined by this equation in the <em>xy</em>-plane and <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> represents the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of this line. Therefore, the slope of line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s also given that line <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math> is perpendicular to line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane. Therefore, the slope of line <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math> is the opposite reciprocal of the slope of line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math>. The opposite reciprocal of <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"negative one seventh\"><mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the slope of line <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"negative one seventh\"><mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the opposite reciprocal of the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept, not the slope, of line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math>, not the slope of line <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the slope of a line that is parallel, not perpendicular, to line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math>.</p>","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> is defined by <math alttext=\"y equals 7 x plus one eighth\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t</mfrac>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Line <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math> is perpendicular to line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane. What is the slope of line <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math>?</p>","type":"mcq","correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1730147357392,"updateDate":1730147357392}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147357392, 1730147357392),
