<p style="text-align: left;">What is the estimated volume, in liters, of the hydrogen when its temperature is <math alttext="500"><mn>500</mn>
</math> kelvins?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"3002ffb4-958a-4819-aac2-a4104d0984f4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"85946d83-79a1-4563-beca-b64878472fa6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 7 Over 500 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>500</mn></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"732945e4-4431-4192-9eb6-485f7a5bdfaf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"28832a0b-86e7-49a2-8b0c-3fc9ffee6a4b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 500 Over 7 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>500</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["732945e4-4431-4192-9eb6-485f7a5bdfaf"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. For the graph shown, the <em>x</em>-axis represents temperature, in kelvins, and the <em>y</em>-axis represents volume, in liters. Therefore, the estimated volume, in liters, of the hydrogen when its temperature is <math alttext="500"><mn>500</mn>
</math> kelvins is represented by the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the point on the graph that has an <em>x</em>-coordinate of <math alttext="500"><mn>500</mn>
</math>. The point on the graph with an <em>x</em>-coordinate of <math alttext="500"><mn>500</mn>
</math> has a <em>y</em>-coordinate of <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math>. Therefore, the estimated volume, in liters, of the hydrogen when its temperature is <math alttext="500"><mn>500</mn>
</math> kelvins is <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
