</math>. Therefore, <math alttext="m equals 2"><mrow>
	<mi>m</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>2</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. It&rsquo;s also given that the graph of <math alttext="y equals g left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> passes through the point <math alttext="left parenthesis 1 comma 14 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. It follows that when <math alttext="x equals 1"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>1</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, <math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 14"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math>. Substituting <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>, <math alttext="14"><mn>14</mn>
</math> for&nbsp;<math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, and <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="m"><mi>m</mi>
</math> in the equation&nbsp;<math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals m x plus b"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math> yields <math alttext="14 equals 2 left parenthesis 1 right parenthesis plus b"><mn>14</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, or <math alttext="14 equals 2 plus b"><mn>14</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>. Subtracting <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> from each side of this equation yields <math alttext="12 equals b"><mrow>
	<mn>12</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>b</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, <math alttext="b equals 12"><mrow>
	<mi>b</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>12</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="m"><mi>m</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="12"><mn>12</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals m x plus b"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math> yields <math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 2 x plus 12"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn></math>. Therefore, the equation that defines <math alttext="g"><mi>g</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 2 x plus 12"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. For this function, the graph of <math alttext="y equals g left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane passes through the point <math alttext="left parenthesis 1 comma 2 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, not <math alttext="left parenthesis 1 comma 14 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. For this function, the graph of <math alttext="y equals g left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane passes through the point <math alttext="left parenthesis 1 comma 4 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, not <math alttext="left parenthesis 1 comma 14 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. For this function, the graph of <math alttext="y equals g left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane passes through the point <math alttext="left parenthesis 1 comma 16 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, not <math alttext="left parenthesis 1 comma 14 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"946ab892","external_id":"75be103e-3a39-4793-99d5-2ecb57774a84","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"9f5768ba-64ce-4a31-a5a0-92c142e140db","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.B.","skill_desc":"Linear functions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">For the linear function <math alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi>\n</math>, the graph of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"y equals g left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane has a slope of <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> and passes through the point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 1 comma 14 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math>. Which equation defines <math alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"295aab16-5162-4500-b58b-ccabaa100d7a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 2 x\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"2357e134-bf37-4271-941c-c78e4d65c9d6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 2 x plus 2\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>